# Activities

Activities are Adafruit IO's list of actions you've taken to create or
delete objects in your Adafruit IO account. Updates are not logged. We store the last 10,000 actions taken for:

* Dashboards
* Blocks
* Feeds
* Groups
* Actions
* Tokens

## All Activities

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span> <code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/activities</code></div>

```shell
curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" \
  https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/activities
```

```python
```

```cpp
```

```ruby
```

> Response Sample

```json
[
  {
    "id": 0,
    "action": "create",
    "model": "Feed",
    "data": "{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Temperature\"}",
    "user_id": 0,
    "created_at": "string",
    "updated_at": "string"
  }
]
```

### Path Parameters

Parameter |   Type  |  Required |       Description
--------- | ------- | --------- | -----------------------
username | string | true | a valid username string


### Query Parameters

Parameter |   Type  |  Required |       Description
--------- | ------- | --------- | -----------------------
start_time | string | false | Start time for filtering, returns records created after given time.
end_time | string | false | End time for filtering, returns records created before give time.
limit | integer | false | Limit the number of records returned (default: 100, maximum: 1000).


## Get Activities by Type

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/activities/{type}</code></div>

```shell
# Returns two records
$ curl -F 'limit=2' -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/activities/{type}
```

```python
```

```cpp
```

```ruby
```

> Response Sample:

```json
[
  {
    "id": 0,
    "action": "create",
    "model": "Feed",
    "data": "{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Temperature\"}",
    "user_id": 0,
    "created_at": "string",
    "updated_at": "string"
  }
]
```

An array of activities, newest first. `action` is `create` or `destroy`. `data` is a JSON-encoded string describing the object at that time.


### Path Parameters

Parameter |   Type  |  Required |       Description
--------- | ------- | --------- | -----------------------
username | string | true | a valid username string
type | string | true | the type of object, case-sensitive: `Feed`, `Group`, `Dashboard`, `Block`, `Trigger` (actions) or `Token`


### Query Parameters

Parameter |   Type  |  Required |       Description
--------- | ------- | --------- | -----------------------
start_time | string | false | Start time for filtering, returns records created after given time.
end_time | string | false | End time for filtering, returns records created before give time.
limit | integer | false | Limit the number of records returned (default: 100, maximum: 1000).


